  "schema_version": 1,
  "comment": "Flips a Spack node's PROVIDER to a native Bazel build without editing the generated spack_graph.lock.json or changing DAG topology. Keys under 'native' map a Spack package name to the Bazel target label that emits a prefix-identical, ABI-identical install tree; spack_to_bazel.py --native-overrides applies these, setting build:native + native_prefix on the matched node. Empty by default: leaf-proof runs opt in explicitly (see run_native_zlib.sh). 'provided_versions' records, per 'native' key, the concrete Spack version the native recipe actually builds (evidenced from its MODULE.bazel source, recipe doc, and capture graph); tools/migration_ledger_check.py and spack_to_bazel.py reject any flip whose provided version differs from the graph node it serves. 'known_version_substitutions' lists the only tolerated mismatches, each tied to a tracker ticket; an entry that no longer matches a real substitution is an error.",
